    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48712.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "It's pretty exciting for us. I have to say we're sort of thrilled. We really are. We're very happy. So and Senator, your ears might have been ringing because we were talking about how you how you really do show up for people. And I want to commend you for that. Regardless of whoever is listening in political affiliation and votes, I consider you a public servant. You don't ask people's affiliation when they call you for constituent service. You don't ask whether or not they voted for you when you show up if they've been flooded or they've had some kind of other catastrophe happen for them. I want to just say that you stand out as a public service for your accessibility and extraordinary ability to be in all places at all times when people need you. I want to just say that.",
