    "turn_text": "is. And I asked you on the show today because you have been candid about your father's story as a Nazi immigrade. In other words, as somebody who left the Nazis and escaped in time and your extraordinary American success story here. But your roots to Israel, your deeply personal historical and familial roots to Israel and you and I together share that and the really the agony of over the last year, what's been happening there, the emergence of anti-Semitism here, that scathing report that came out on Friday about Columbia having to redo a lot of what they're about because of all the Jewish kids there that have been physically taunted and and basically segregated and attacked for their Jewish faith. The overwhelming amount of Jewish kids now on college campuses who won't wear a Jewish star or a high because they're afraid of being singled out as a Jew or called a Zionist, which somehow became a bad word. And then we have the very real and current present news of an American, a boy whose parents spoke at the Democratic National Convention, you were there. They believed he was alive, he was alive, and he and five others were shot by Hamas because they might have been rescued. And you sit at the juncture, you're on the Judiciary Committee, you're a U.S. Senator, you've made countless trips to the Middle East and Ukraine. So you tell us from 40,000 feet, what's going on? President Biden saying Netanyahu isn't doing enough, but he's not he's not our president. In other words, you know, we can't do anything about the fact that Israel has a coalition government and his coalition is still standing behind him. That's their system. And until they have an election, that's it. They got him. Well, I just want to hear your thoughts on all of this. It's been a terrible weekend. Terrible.",
