    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "You know, Senator Blumenthal, yesterday spoke to my family in Israel, and my family said to me, she said, it felt like October 8th yesterday, okay? It was very raw, very bad. And all these strikes and her kids aren't going to school today because the high schools, the teachers aren't showing up and all this other stuff. catastrophic for the country. And I said to her, well, what is it about? And she told me that it's really about whether or not people should just say they're giving in to whatever Hamas wants and then do what they want the next day after they get the hostages back or stand for these principles of saying, no, we're not going to let you have the Philadelphia Corridor and all these other things. And a lot of people in Israel are like, just give Hamas whatever they want because we need to get our hostages back. And the day after we get them back, you know what, maybe it's all bets are off. I don't know. What do you think? I mean, that's what's going on in Israel. That's the strife in Israel right now. That's what the protests were about.",
